#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:4
msgid "Configuration Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:6
msgid ""
"Syncthing ships with a set of default values designed to work well for most "
"users under common circumstances. However, there are a number of "
"configuration options that can be tweaked to improve performance or to "
"reduce resource consumption. This article makes recommendations, but you "
"will need to experiment to find the best settings for your particular setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:13
msgid "Tuning for High Performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:15
msgid ""
"You have resources to spare and want to optimize for performance. To begin "
"with, make sure you are running a 64 bit build and that the index database "
"is on an SSD. First some general options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:19 ../../../users/tuning.rst:136
msgid ":opt:`progressUpdateIntervalS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:20
msgid ""
"Set to -1 to disable progress updates. Time spent on progress updates is "
"time not spent on syncing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:23
msgid ":opt:`setLowPriority`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:24
msgid ""
"Set to false to run Syncthing with normal priority. This may allow Syncthing "
"to use more CPU time, which can improve performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:27 ../../../users/tuning.rst:140
msgid ":opt:`maxFolderConcurrency`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:28
msgid ""
"Find an appropriate setting for the number of folders to sync concurrently, "
"taking into account the inherent concurrency of the underlying storage "
"system. If two folders are on the same underlying spinning disk, syncing "
"them concurrently will be a strict loss of performance. If the underlying "
"storage is a large array of disk, then syncing many folders concurrently may "
"be beneficial."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:35 ../../../users/tuning.rst:143
msgid ":opt:`maxConcurrentIncomingRequestKiB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:36
msgid ""
"This sets the maximum amount of data being processed (loaded from disk and "
"transmitted over the network) concurrently at any given time. This is a "
"global limiter, not per folder. If you have a lot of folders and/or a lot of "
"devices and memory to spare you may want to increase this value. The default "
"is 256 MiB, consider values of 1024 MiB or more."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:43
msgid "These options are folder specific and should be set on each folder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:45 ../../../users/tuning.rst:149
msgid ":opt:`fsWatcherEnabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:46
msgid ""
"When possible, using filesystem notifications avoids unnecessary I/O in "
"large periodic scans. Changes are detected faster using notifications than "
"scans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:50
msgid ":opt:`copiers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:51
msgid ""
"The number of routines used for the copy stage of file syncing. Similar to "
"other concurrency options, if there are a lot of files to sync and if the I/"
"O system can handle it it you may see increased performance by increasing "
"this value. The default is system dependent, somewhere between 1 and the "
"number of CPU cores available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:57
msgid ":opt:`hashers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:58
msgid ""
"When hashing locally changed files, the number of hashing routines to use. "
"Higher values mean more I/O and CPU load and may increase performance when "
"there are a lot of files to hash, assuming I/O bandwidth and CPU are "
"available. The default is system dependent, somewhere between 1 and the "
"number of CPU cores available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:64 ../../../users/tuning.rst:157
msgid ":opt:`pullerMaxPendingKiB`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:65
msgid ""
"The maximum amount of data to have outstanding requests for at any given "
"time. Higher values may improve performance, especially if the network or I/"
"O latency is high. The default is 32 MiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:69 ../../../users/tuning.rst:161
msgid ":opt:`scanProgressIntervalS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:70
msgid ""
"Providing the GUI with scan progress updates is not very expensive, but is "
"effort that could be spent on something more productive. If you don't need "
"to see scan progress, set this to -1 to disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:74
msgid ":opt:`maxConcurrentWrites`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:75
msgid ""
"Synchting limits the number of outstanding write system calls at any given "
"time to avoid overloading the I/O system. If you increased copiers, "
"outstanding network requests, or other settings that increase the number of "
"concurrent writes, you may need to increase this value. The default is 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:81
msgid ":opt:`disableFsync`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:82
msgid ""
"Syncthing calls ``fsync()`` on files and directories after syncing them to "
"ensure they are safe and sound on stable storage. This is a good thing, but "
"it can be expensive. If you have a lot of files to sync and/or a lot of I/O "
"bandwidth available, you may see a performance increase by disabling "
"``fsync()``. This is not recommended for most setups, as you are increasing "
"the risk of data loss in case of a power outage or system crash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:90
msgid ":opt:`blockPullOrder`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:91
msgid ""
"Syncthing by default uses a pseudo-random block order when pulling in order "
"to distribute load over multiple devices better. If you are generally "
"downloading files from only one device, and if you have spinning disks as "
"the underlying storage, you may see a performance increase by setting this "
"to ``inOrder``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:97 ../../../users/tuning.rst:165
msgid ":opt:`copyRangeMethod`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:98
msgid ""
"If your underlying filesystem supports it, you may see a performance "
"increase by enabling a copy-on-write method, as it reduces the amount of "
"data actually copied on disk when syncing files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:102 ../../../users/tuning.rst:169
msgid ":opt:`caseSensitiveFS`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:103
msgid ""
"If your underlying filesystem is case sensitive, you may see a performance "
"increase by enabling this option. This disables a number of safety checks "
"that are required for case insensitive filesystems, and can cause data loss "
"if your underlying filesystem is *not* in fact case sensitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:109
msgid ""
":opt:`syncOwnership`/:opt:`syncXattrs`, :opt:`sendOwnership`/:opt:"
"`sendXattrs`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:110
msgid ""
"Use these if they are required for your use case, but keep in mind they have "
"a fairly high performance cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:113
msgid "For devices, consider the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:115 ../../../users/tuning.rst:178
msgid ":opt:`numConnections`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:116
msgid ""
"Set at or above the number of CPU cores available. This allows maximum "
"concurrency for TLS connections and may improve performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:119 ../../../users/tuning.rst:182
msgid "Other things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:121
msgid ""
"``GOMEMLIMIT`` and ``GOGC``: These environment variables can be used to "
"control the garbage collector. For large setups, setting ``GOMEMLIMIT`` to "
"the desired max amount of memory Syncthing should use can improve "
"performance. The reason is that this reduces garbage collector frequency "
"during lower memory usage. Read more in the `Go GC guide <https://golang.org/"
"doc/gc-guide>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:129
msgid "Tuning for Low Resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:131
msgid ""
"You have limited resources and want Syncthing to use as few as possible. You "
"care less about performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:134
msgid "General options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:137
msgid ""
"Set to -1 to disable progress updates. Progress updates aren't absolutely "
"essential and consume some amount of CPU and memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:141
msgid "Set to 1 to sync folders sequentially, reducing the peak memory usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:144
msgid ""
"Set to 32 MiB to reduce the amount of memory used for buffering responses to "
"incoming requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:147
msgid "Folders options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:150
msgid ""
"If possible, using the filesystem notifications is more efficient than doing "
"full periodic scans."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:153
msgid ":opt:`copiers`, :opt:`hashers`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:154
msgid ""
"Set to 1 to reduce the amount of concurrency when syncing and hashing a "
"folder, reducing peak memory usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:158
msgid ""
"Set to 16 MiB to reduce the amount of memory used for buffering while "
"syncing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:162
msgid ""
"Set to -1 to disable scan progress updates. Keeping track of scan progress "
"uses memory and CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:166
msgid ""
"If your underlying filesystem supports it, using copyrange is more efficient "
"than having Syncthing do the data copying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:170
msgid ""
"If your underlying filesystem is case sensitive, set this to skip a number "
"of checks which have a memory cost due to caching. These checks are required "
"for case insensitive filesystems, and disabling them can cause data loss if "
"your underlying filesystem is *not* in fact case sensitive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:176
msgid "Device options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:179
msgid ""
"Set to 1 to reduce the amount of overhead per device, as each connection has "
"a memory and CPU cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:184
msgid "``GOMEMLIMIT`` and ``GOGC``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:185
msgid ""
"These environment variables can be used to control the garbage collector. "
"For small setups, setting ``GOMEMLIMIT`` to the desired max amount of memory "
"Syncthing should use can make the garbage collector adhere more closely to "
"the desired limit. Read more in the `Go GC guide <https://golang.org/doc/gc-"
"guide>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:191
msgid "``GOMAXPROCS``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:192
msgid ""
"This environment variable can be used to control the maximum number number "
"concurrently running threads Syncthing uses. Setting it to 1 (or any number "
"lower than your actual number of cores) will reduce the amount of CPU used "
"by Syncthing at any given moment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:198
msgid "Tuning for LAN-only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:200
msgid ""
"You are paranoid about security and/or privacy, and want to keep Syncthing's "
"communication constrained to your local network only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:203
msgid "For restricting sync traffic to only LAN:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:205
msgid ":opt:`relaysEnabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:206
msgid ""
"Set to false to disable relaying sync traffic through servers other than "
"your sync partners. When relays are used, those that you connect to can see "
"your device ID and public IP address, but not the synchronized data, as that "
"is encrypted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:211
msgid ":ref:`unknown-suspicious-address`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:213
msgid ":opt:`natEnabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:214
msgid ""
"Set to false to disable opening up UPnP and NAT-PMP port mappings and "
"pinholes, and to disable hole punching. This reduces the ability for sync "
"partners to connect on the Internet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:218
msgid "For restricting other things to only LAN:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:220
msgid ":opt:`globalAnnounceEnabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:221
msgid ""
"Set to false to disable use of Global Discovery servers, which know your "
"device ID and public IP address when being used. The discovery servers are "
"used by your sync partners to discover your IP address from your device ID."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:226
msgid ""
"On Android, local discovery is known to usually not work, so either global "
"discovery or hardcoding IP addresses is often required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:229
msgid ":opt:`urAccepted`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:230
msgid ""
"Set to -1 to disable usage reporting. When usage reporting is enabled, usage "
"reporting servers can know your public IP address, :opt:`urUniqueID`, and "
"(obviously) the contents of the usage report (which depend on the version "
"you chose)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:235
msgid ":opt:`crashReportingEnabled`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:236
msgid ""
"Set to false to disable automatic crash reporting. Crash reporting servers "
"can know your public IP address, the version of Syncthing that crashed, and "
"the username and hostname of the machine that Syncthing was built on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:240
msgid ":doc:`crashrep`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:242
msgid ":opt:`autoUpgradeIntervalH`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:243
msgid ""
"Set to 0 to disable automatic upgrades. Syncthing will still automatically "
"contact the Internet to check for upgrades when you open up the Web GUI, so "
"it knows when to show the upgrade button, unless you follow the procedure "
"for :opt:`releasesURL`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:248
msgid ":opt:`releasesURL`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:249
msgid ""
"Unset (set to blank) to disable upgrade checks. With upgrade checks "
"disabled, to upgrade Syncthing, you have to manually replace the executable "
"and restart Syncthing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../users/tuning.rst:253
msgid ""
"If it's not obvious, do *not* hardcode non-LAN IP addresses, if you want to "
"keep LAN-only."
msgstr ""
